[Opening "Grünfeld Defense: Brinckmann Attack"]

{Grünfeld Defense: Brinckmann Attack. A slight inaccuracy in move order — the bishop is better placed before this pawn commits.}
1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Bf4 Bg7 5. e3 c5 {Book so far. The plan is the usual one: finish development, then decide which side to open.} 6. dxc5 Qa5 7. cxd5 Nxd5 8. Qxd5 ! Bxc3+ {The point of the whole plan. Material is level, but only one side has a target to attack.} (8... Qxa2 Rb1 Qa1 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. bxc3 Qxc3+ 10. Ke2 Qxa1 11. Be5 Qb1 ?! 12. Bxh8 Be6 13. Qd3 Qxa2+ 14. Kf3 f6 15. Bg7 Nd7 16. Kg3 Rc8 17. c6 Rxc6 18. Qd4 Rd6 19. Qb4 Rd1 20. Nf3 Qc2 21. Nd4 Qc7+ 22. f4 Qc1 23. Bh6 Bd5 24. Kf2 Rd2+ 25. Ne2 Bc6 26. h3 Nc5 27. Kg3 Rxe2 28. Bxe2 Qxh1 29. Bf3 Bxf3 30. Kxf3 Qd1+ 31. Kg3 b6 32. Kh2 Qh5 33. Qa3 Qxh6 34. Qxa7 Qh5 35. Qxb6 Kf7 36. Qd8 Qf5 37. Qh8 g5 38. fxg5 fxg5 39. Kg1 Qb1+ 40. Kh2 Qe4 41. Qc3 Nd7 42. Qb3+ Qe6 43. Qd3 Qd6+ 44. Qxd6 exd6 45. Kg3 Ne5 46. e4 Kf6 47. Kf2 h5 48. Ke3 Nd7 49. Kd4 Ke6 50. g3 Nf6 51. Ke3 Ke5 {The rest is technique, which is another way of saying it still has to be played accurately.} 52. Ke2 1-0
